From 454a0f88ba705aaae23a4a002294b426fa37ff51 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 06:56:58 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Add gs_quant.research: academic toolkit for data,
 valuation and strategies

New local package (numpy/pandas/scipy/statsmodels only, no Marquee session
needed) implementing methods from peer-reviewed research:

- data_management: price audits, look-ahead-free cleaning, Hampel/MAD
  outlier filter, winsorization, point-in-time alignment of fundamentals
- risk: Ledoit-Wolf shrinkage, EWMA (RiskMetrics), Marchenko-Pastur
  denoising, historical/Gaussian/Cornish-Fisher VaR, Expected Shortfall
- performance: Sharpe, Sortino, Calmar, Omega, IR, probabilistic and
  deflated Sharpe ratios, minimum track record length
- valuation: bond price/yield/duration/convexity, Black-Scholes-Merton
  price, Greeks and implied vol, Gordon growth, DCF, CAPM
- factors: CAPM/Fama-French regressions with Newey-West errors,
  Fama-MacBeth cross-sectional regressions
- portfolio: 1/N, inverse vol, risk parity, HRP, min variance,
  mean-variance, max Sharpe, Black-Litterman, Kelly, efficient frontier
- signals: time-series and cross-sectional momentum, short-term reversal,
  moving-average rules, low volatility, volatility targeting
- backtest: lagged execution with weight drift and turnover costs,
  walk-forward allocation, purged k-fold splits
- demo: runnable end-to-end example (python -m gs_quant.research.demo)

Includes a Spanish README with best practices and full bibliography,
Sphinx docs page, and 97 unit tests checking formulas against reference
implementations, textbook values and finite differences.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
