From d102969e5474906d871fd2aef60c70772664b881 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 14:10:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Add growth company valuation and long-term quality-growth
 strategy

New modules in gs_quant.research:

- fundamentals: point-in-time annual fundamentals (first-reported values,
  filing dates), growth/profitability/quality metrics (ROIC, gross
  profitability, accruals, asset growth), Piotroski F-score, Mohanram
  G-score, and an SEC EDGAR companyfacts parser/downloader
- growth_valuation: growth DCF with faded growth, sales-to-capital
  reinvestment and value-driver terminal value; reverse DCF (market-implied
  growth); residual income model; CAPM/WACC with Blume beta; bear/base/bull
  probability-weighted valuation with margin of safety
- growth_strategy: LongTermGrowthStrategy screening the fastest growers on
  entry rules (ROIC > WACC, margin of safety, F-score), composite growth/
  quality/valuation/momentum score, entry/hold hysteresis to cut turnover,
  risk-parity weights with a position cap and cash when few names qualify,
  backtest, and export to a gs_quant.markets PositionSet
- growth_demo: runnable walk-through on a synthetic universe or user CSVs

Also fixes weight assembly in rolling_allocation: DataFrame.from_dict
silently dropped rebalance dates with an empty selection (which must mean
"all cash") and could reorder rows; replaced with weights_frame.

Adds 38 tests (135 total) and a Spanish README section with methodology,
real-data usage and references.

